  "releaseNotes": "2.2.1 reduces managed allocation when preparing byte-mode GNU/POSIX regular-expression input by allocating final decoded arrays directly. Physical reference-host validation of a 1 MiB prepared input measured a 47.36% allocation reduction, from about 19.01 MiB to 10.00 MiB per preparation, with materially improved construction time and no changes to UTF-8 decoding, matching, capture, cancellation, diagnostic, or resource-limit semantics.",
